  "published": "2026-10-21T06:11:49.233Z",
  "readmeFile": "PackageReadme.md",
  "releaseNotes": "Requires TokenGuard.Core 1.3.0 or later, and OpenAI 2.14.0 or later. The summarizer implements Core's public ILlmSummarizer contract, so Core builds its transcript, request budget and response checks; a summarizer answer that is a refusal throws InvalidOperationException with the refusal text.\n\nBehavior changes come from TokenGuard.Core 1.3.0, with no signature changes: a recorded tool result above a token limit is stored shortened; the compaction strategy receives its budget on the estimate scale, inverted from the provider correction; pretty-printed JSON is charged for its whitespace; a tool result is masked only when its placeholder is smaller; the summarizer request is built to a token budget and its output cap is twice the target; summarizer diagnostics name the summarizer type and normalize finish reasons. Prepared views can differ from those of 1.2.0 for the same history.\n\nKnown limits: one ConversationContext is for one caller at a time, and overlapping calls are detected on a best-effort basis; token estimates leave out request overhead such as tool schemas until the first provider report; with the tool result limit turned off, one tool result larger than the window cannot be fitted and the prepare returns CompactionInsufficient; the package targets net10.0 only.\n\nFull details: https://github.com/svetstoykov/TokenGuard/blob/main/CHANGELOG.md",
